-- title:
--   Weight 2 or p+1 eigensystem placement at p=3
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass model over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta(W) \neq 0$ which is semistable in the sense that no prime dividing $\Delta(W)$ divides $c_4(W)$, and whose $p$-torsion over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is irreducible in the sense that the $p$-torsion subgroup of the points of $W_{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole group. Assume further that for every valuation subring $A$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, any $p$-torsion point fixed by every element of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ is zero. Let $N' \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N'$, and assume $5 \leq p$ or that some prime $q \mid N'$ satisfies $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S_0$, let $k'$ be an integer with $2 \leq k' \leq p+1$, let $i \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $\mathfrak{m}'$ be a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[T_\ell, U_q]$ acting on $S_{k'}(\Gamma_0(N'))$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ generated by $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$, $\ell \notin S_0$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$, $q \notin S_0$) with $p \in \mathfrak{m}'$ and $T_\ell - \ell^i a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}'$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$. The conclusion is that at least one of the two untwisted placements exists: either a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2$ of the corresponding Hecke algebra in weight $2$ with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_2$ and $T_\ell - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}_2$ for all such $\ell$, or a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_3$ of the Hecke algebra in weight $p+1$ with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_3$ and $T_\ell - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}_3$ for all such $\ell$.
--
--   This is the $p = 3$ instance of the weight-optimisation step in the style of Serre's conjecture and Edixhoven's weight analysis: an eigensystem matching the mod-$p$ representation of $W$ up to a twist by $\ell^i$, realised in some weight $k'$ with $2 \leq k' \leq p+1$, is moved to the untwisted eigensystem in weight $2$ or in weight $p+1$, the level $N'$ and the excluded set $S_0$ being unchanged. Since $p = 3$ here, the disjunctive hypothesis amounts to the existence of a prime divisor $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$ of $N'$; the result feeds the residual modularity statement for semistable curves with no inertia-fixed $3$-torsion.
